## FINDING 1 (T2, the run's main deliverable) — a wired miner that could not, in principle, produce what it was for

`desks/mt5/side_channels/central_bank_miner.py` was wired into run_all_miners.py and listed
zero-yield by check_miner_conversion (20+ rows, 0 survivors/14d). Reading the file instead of
trusting the fence's source-level verdict: it scraped each bank's HTML LANDING PAGE, kept the
first 2000 chars after tag-stripping (navigation chrome), counted policy keywords, and **emitted
no timestamp at all** — so nothing it produced could ever become an event series, which is
precisely what the two absent families need. Second defect: `_extract_symbols` substring-matched
instrument tickers against a central bank's page; "EURUSD" does not appear on federalreserve.gov,
so it returned [] every run and the fallback emitted **"USDUSD"** for the Fed. Positive control
against `git show HEAD:` of the old file reproduces both.

REPAIRED IN THE SAME CHANGE (detect implies repair). Dated RSS/RDF feeds, probed live and all
keyless 200: Fed press_monetary.xml, ECB rss/press.html, BoJ whatsnew.xml, BoE rss/news, BoC
press-releases, BIS cbspeeches.rss. BIS is RDF `dc:date`, NOT `pubDate` — a pubDate-only reader
returns zero rows there and reads as an empty feed, so both tag families are parsed. Instruments
now derive from the speaking bank's CURRENCY. An undated item is DROPPED, never stamped `now`
(L1.46). **Measured: 162 dated documents, 0 undated, 2026-03-18 -> 2026-08-26, BoE 50 / BoJ 47 /
BIS 25 / Fed 15 / ECB 15 / BoC 10** -> desks/mt5/data/intelligence/central_banks/cb_documents.jsonl.
7 regression tests, each naming its defect. Gates green.

RESIDUALS, stated so nothing reads as success: **RBA 403 from this box under two UAs — AUD has
NO central-bank coverage and the row is kept so the miner shouts about it every run**; SNB not
routed (CHF uncovered); only 2/162 rows carry a policy signal because the feeds give titles, not
bodies — **this is an attention stream, not yet a hawkish/dovish series**; and RSS is a rolling
window, so this axis **cannot backfill** and accrues only forward. That last one is the price of
the six months the miner sat broken, and it is the argument for reading the reader whenever a
fence calls a source zero-yield.

## FINDING 2 (T2) — the §33 backlog was 68% PHANTOM, and the mechanism is a one-line parser rule

The gate opened this run demanding 22 dispositions "weighted 48". Fifteen of those cards ALREADY
CARRIED a valid future deferral — on the line BELOW the heading, where
`libs/research/mine_conversion.parse_dispositions` cannot see it. Measured directly: the identical
tag parses to `('deferred','2026-09-05',2)` on the heading line and to `('', '')` one line down.
This is the known heading-line rule (R0514/R0617 family) and it had been inflating the desk's
convert-first directive by 3x, aiming every digger's FIRST effort at work that was not owed.
Card-side fix applied (the KR-s4 precedent; the parser fix stays engineering-owned): 15 orphaned
tags moved onto their headings. **22 -> 7.**

The remaining 7 were real debt and are now disposed on measured evidence, not rubber-stamped:
S2 GitHub (api.github.com keyless 200, total_count=646 for topic:mql5 — route live, corpus owed),
S3 TradingView (200; **merged into S12 as the same ground described twice — recorded as one item,
not counted as two**), S4 QuantConnect (robots read: `/api` BARRED, public pages open — the same
boundary shape as MQL5), S5/S7/S8 deferred with dates and named skip reasons, S6 wired above.
**Gate now reads BACKLOG-CLEAR: all 29 carded finds disposed.**

